--- !u!114 &1688734030145796371
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6647370592428966729}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7045ec06c0f03f547825a62b228d5dae, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  globe: {fileID: 7139848423845056624}
  titleText: {fileID: 0}
  instructionText: {fileID: 0}
  narrationSource: {fileID: 0}
  steps:
  - title: Our Earth
    instruction: Observe the globe and notice its spherical shape.
    voiceOver: A globe is a spherical model of Earth. It helps us understand places,
      directions and how our planet moves.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Explore
    instruction: Drag to rotate. Pinch or use the mouse wheel to zoom.
    voiceOver: Rotate the globe to explore continents and oceans from every direction.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Equator and Poles
    instruction: Study the equator, poles and tilted axis.
    voiceOver: The equator divides Earth into northern and southern hemispheres.
      Earth's axis is tilted by about twenty-three and a half degrees.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Latitude and Longitude
    instruction: Turn on the coordinate grid and locate a point.
    voiceOver: Latitude measures north or south of the equator. Longitude measures
      east or west of the Prime Meridian.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Hemispheres
    instruction: Compare Earth's northern, southern, eastern and western halves.
    voiceOver: The equator separates north and south. The Prime Meridian helps separate
      east and west.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Real Places
    instruction: Tap glowing pins to identify locations and coordinates.
    voiceOver: Every location can be described using a latitude and longitude coordinate.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Day and Night
    instruction: Observe the illuminated side and dark side as Earth rotates.
    voiceOver: Day and night occur because Earth rotates. The side facing the Sun
      has daylight while the opposite side experiences night.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - title: Review
    instruction: Review the overlays, then continue to the learning check.
    voiceOver: You explored the equator, poles, hemispheres, coordinates, axis tilt,
      locations, and day and night.
    narration: {fileID: 0}
    onEnter:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  currentStep: 0
